# Mark binary assets so git never attempts diffs, merges, or CRLF translation
# on them. 367 asset files were tracked when this rule was written; Phase 1
# §1.8's `git filter-repo` purge stripped those from every commit in this range,
# and Phase 1 re-encoded and committed the 10 survivors now under
# assets/animations/.
*.gif  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.wav  binary

# Normalize line endings on text.
*.go       text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
Makefile   text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf

# NOTE: these are deliberately NOT Git LFS objects. See AGENTS.md
# ("Do not introduce Git LFS") — an LFS pointer would be silently embedded by
# assets/assets.go's //go:embed in place of the GIF, and every scene would render
# flat navy. That embed is live as of Phase 2; assets.TestEmbeddedAssetsAreRealGifs
# checks the magic bytes so the failure cannot ship quietly.
